You are an expert game developer. Build a complete, playable web-based clone of "Last War: Survival Game" as a single self-contained HTML file that runs in a browser with no build step.

Use vanilla JavaScript, HTML5 Canvas (2D context) for the runner gameplay, and DOM/CSS overlays for menus, HUD, and the base-building meta layer. No external libraries, no CDNs, no image or audio files fetched from URLs. All art is procedurally drawn with Canvas primitives or CSS gradients and shapes.

Target 60 FPS on desktop and mobile. Support both mouse and touch drag for steering and tap for UI. The canvas must resize responsively while keeping world proportions locked.

The game has two connected modes: (A) a top-down auto-runner shooter where a squad of soldiers advances up a lane, and (B) a persistent base-building meta layer where the player upgrades buildings, trains troops, and unlocks progression. The player toggles between modes with buttons on the home screen.

RUNNER MODE (core loop, must feel polished):

Camera is a fixed top-down 3/4 perspective. The lane scrolls downward while the squad appears to run upward. Lane width is 6 world units. Base scroll speed 8 u/s, accelerating to 14 u/s by level end.

The squad is rendered as a triangular formation of small circular soldiers with rifles. Starting count is 5. Max count on screen is 60, overflow banked as a counter.

Player controls: drag horizontally anywhere on the canvas to steer the whole squad left or right. Movement uses easing, not snapping. Vertical drag does nothing.

Auto-fire: every soldier fires a small yellow projectile at the nearest enemy every 0.35 seconds. Projectile speed 20 u/s. Damage scales with current weapon tier.

Weapon tiers 1 through 6: pistol, SMG, rifle, shotgun (3-pellet spread), rocket launcher (splash radius 2), minigun (fire rate 0.1s). Upgrades apply to the entire squad.

Gates: every 6 to 10 seconds, the lane presents a pair of gates spanning the lane width. Gates are translucent glowing rectangles the squad must pass through. Only the gate a soldier crosses is applied to that soldier.

Gate types: additive (+3, +5, +8), multiplicative (x2, x3), subtractive (-4, -6), divisive (/2, /3), weapon-upgrade (grants next tier for 10 seconds), shield (grants +1 HP layer to each soldier).

Gate pairs must offer meaningful choice: never pair two positive gates of equal value. Typical pairings: x2 vs +10, x3 vs +20, weapon-up vs +8, shield vs x2. Layout varies and escalates per level.
